2. LOCATION OF ATTRIBUTION

For a publicly accessible website, application, service, or product, the
required attribution must be reasonably accessible to users. It may be placed
in the user interface, footer, About screen, Credits screen, documentation, or
another comparably visible location.

Attribution that exists only in minified source code, hidden metadata, commit
history, or a location not reasonably discoverable by users does not satisfy
this requirement for a public-facing product.

